Package: importABCatlas
Title: Release-Aware Import of Allen Brain Cell Atlas Data into R
Version: 0.2.0.9007
Authors@R: person("Maintainer", "To be completed", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "maintainer@example.org")
Description: Provides release-aware access to Allen Brain Cell Atlas metadata
    and selected H5AD expression from R. The package validates identifiers and
    joins, reports exact source files and disk requirements before download,
    resumes interrupted transfers, and returns sparse matrices or optional
    Seurat and Bioconductor objects. A private Python environment is prepared
    automatically on first use, so users do not need to install or configure
    Python manually.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: jsonlite, Matrix, methods, reticulate (>= 1.41.0), stats, utils
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.1.0), roxygen2, SeuratObject (>= 5.0.0),
    SingleCellExperiment, S4Vectors, SpatialExperiment, SummarizedExperiment
SystemRequirements: Internet access is required once to prepare the private Python environment
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://github.com/me37uday/importABCatlas
BugReports: https://github.com/me37uday/importABCatlas/issues
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
